{"name":"Czech Bakery","hex":"#dec9a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bakery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place in which bread (and often other baked goods such as cakes) is baked and/or sold.","The trade of a baker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bakery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bakery","blocks":[{"text":"A bakery is an establishment that produces and sells flour-based baked goods made in an oven such as bread, cookies, cakes, doughnuts, pizzas, bagels, pastries, and pies. Some retail bakeries are also categorized as cafés, serving coffee and tea to customers who wish to consume the baked goods on the premises. In some countries, a distinction is made between bakeries, which primarily sell breads, and pâtisseries, which primarily sell sweet baked goods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Belgium_2013_%2811620905224%29.jpg/330px-Belgium_2013_%2811620905224%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakery"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg/500px-Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg/1280px-Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg/500px-Bakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bakery sales counter in Paris.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABakery_sales_counter_in_Paris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Paneum_-_%C3%84gypten_B%C3%A4ckerszene_1.jpg/500px-Paneum_-_%C3%84gypten_B%C3%A